  <prompt>The visualization types drifted: VisualHost's local types/index.ts is a 13-member VisualType superset fork of the shared lib's stale 8-member ChartDefinitionTypes; EventDueDateCard is physically duplicated in VisualHost + ui-components. Make @spaarke/visuals the single owner and reconcile the stale copies.</prompt>
  <role>Front-end engineer resolving type/component duplication</role>
  <goal>One canonical VisualType/IChartDefinition/ICardConfig/DrillInteraction and one EventDueDateCard, owned by @spaarke/visuals; ui-components re-exports or removes its stale copies; no consumer breaks.</goal>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="design">@spaarke/visuals is the single owner. ui-components re-exports for back-compat or removes if unused.</constraint>
    <constraint source="shared-surface">Verify no other consumer of the ui-components stale types/EventDueDateCard breaks. Coordinate with PR #508.</constraint>
  </constraints>
  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/types/ChartDefinitionTypes.ts</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/types/DrillInteractionTypes.ts</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/EventDueDateCard/</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>
  <steps>
    <step id="1">Confirm @spaarke/visuals owns the full (13-member) VisualType + related interfaces.</step>
    <step id="2">Replace the shared-lib stale types with re-exports from @spaarke/visuals (or remove if unused); grep all consumers first.</step>
    <step id="3">De-duplicate EventDueDateCard: keep the @spaarke/visuals copy; re-export or remove the ui-components copy.</step>
    <step id="4">Build all affected packages/consumers; confirm nothing breaks.</step>
  </steps>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>One VisualType definition repo-wide.</criterion>
    <criterion>One EventDueDateCard.</criterion>
    <criterion>No consumer build breaks (verified by grep + build).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
</task>
